Note on PyAV's bundled native libraries: the av 19.0.1 manylinux aarch64 wheel ships shared
libraries in av.libs/, including FFmpeg (libavcodec, libavformat, libavutil, libavfilter,
libavdevice, libswscale, libswresample), libx264, libx265, libvpx, libdav1d, libopus, libwebp,
SVT-AV1, libvmaf, GnuTLS/Nettle/GMP and X11/XCB libraries. The wheel's licence file covers PyAV only.
According to the official repositories, FFmpeg is LGPL-2.1-or-later by default and becomes
GPL-2.0-or-later when built with GPL components, and x264 and x265 are GPL-2.0. The bundled build
includes x264 and x265, so treat the FFmpeg libraries in this wheel as GPL-licensed until a legal
review confirms otherwise (OPEN-QUESTIONS Q9). The bundle is built for and deployed to your own
account; this repository does not distribute it.

